	"title"		"GK2 Performance"
	"changenote"		"v1.1.0: much less stutter. No more hitches in the first seconds after loading (the loading screen stays up about 5 s longer until everything is loaded). Buildings, trees and NPCs near the screen now load a little at a time instead of all in one frame, and NPCs load before they walk into view. No freeze the first time a worker starts a craft near you. Garbage collection mostly happens during door fades now. A slow frame no longer makes the next one slow too. The inventory window and item cells for big chests are prepared behind the loading screen. A game update now only turns off the fix it affects instead of the whole mod."
	"description"		"Walking judders, doors freeze the game, NPCs pop in and opening a chest stutters?
This mod removes those hitches without changing how the game looks or plays.

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Smooth walking:[/b] the character and camera no longer judder while you walk
[*][b]Less stutter while exploring:[/b] buildings, stations, trees and props load before they come on screen, a little at a time instead of all in one frame
[*][b]NPCs and workers:[/b] load before they walk into view instead of at the last moment
[*][b]Area preloading:[/b] everything an area needs is prepared behind the loading screen, so the first seconds of play are smooth (the loading screen takes a few seconds longer)
[*][b]Doors and stairs:[/b] no more 0.5–1 s freeze when you use a door or staircase within the same area
[*][b]Fewer random hitches:[/b] garbage collection happens during door fades, and game managers that the game would search for mid-play (for example the first time a worker starts a craft) are set up behind the loading screen
[*][b]No knock-on hitches:[/b] after a slow frame, the game's world logic catches up over the next frames instead of all at once; no game time is lost
[*][b]Instant pause menu:[/b] the ~0.5 s delay on Esc is gone (this disables the bug reporter and hides its button)
[*][b]Faster menus:[/b] menus, the inventory window and the item cells for big chests are prepared in advance
[*][b]Steady camera:[/b] opening a chest while walking no longer makes the camera jump
[*][b]Smoother chests with [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3806668942]No More Running Back[/url]:[/b] no freeze when a chest opens in a big storage area, and no second hitch right after
[*]Less CPU wasted on the game's log messages
[/list]
All time budgets are per frame, so slower PCs spread the work over a few more frames instead of freezing longer.

[h2]Measured[/h2]
Same save, same scripted run (walk through the village and port, doors, chests, pause menu):
[list]
[*]Door out / in: 1.0 s / 0.9 s freeze → hidden in the fade
[*]Pause menu: 269 ms → 12 ms
[*]Walking: frames over twice the usual frame time 36 → 6, frames over 25 ms 5 → 2
[*]Yard chest (21 storages): 284 ms → 177 ms
[*]Worker starting a craft near you: ~45 ms → no hitch
[/list]

[h2]Not fixed[/h2]
[list]
[*]The game streams every sound from disk; starting some sounds costs ~10 ms, which a mod can't change
[*]With No More Running Back, the first chest of a session still takes ~0.3 s (first draw of the window plus that mod's setup)
[*]Busy areas like the yard are limited by rendering; the mod doesn't change graphics
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*]Tested with No More Running Back, [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3809824680]GK2 Sort To Nearby Chests[/url], Better Auto Crafting and GK2 Move Stations
[*]No More Running Back is optional; without it everything else works the same
[/list]

[h2]Safety[/h2]
[list]
[*]Never reads or writes save data; add or remove it at any time, including mid-save
[*]No visual changes
[*]If a game update changes something one fix relies on, only that fix switches off and the rest keep working
[/list]

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*][url=https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx/releases/latest]BepInEx 5[/url]
[/list]

[h2]Install[/h2]
[b]Workshop:[/b] subscribe; with the GK2 Workshop auto-loader installed, it loads on the next game start

[b]Manual:[/b] copy the [i]BepInEx[/i] folder from
[code]steamapps\workshop\content\4358690\3809616755[/code]
into the game folder (Steam Library → right-click Graveyard Keeper 2 → Manage → Browse local files); merge the folders

Game folder after a manual install:
[code]
Graveyard Keeper 2
└─ BepInEx
   └─ plugins
      └─ GK2Performance
         └─ GK2Performance.dll   ← new
[/code]

[h2]Settings[/h2]
[list]
[*][i]BepInEx\config\gk2.performance.cfg[/i] is created on first start
[*]Every feature can be switched off on its own; [i]EnableOptimizations = false[/i] turns everything off
[*]Changes apply after restarting the game
[/list]

[h2]Uninstall[/h2]
Unsubscribe, and delete [i]BepInEx\plugins\GK2Performance[/i] if you installed manually.

[h2]About[/h2]
Made with Claude Opus 5.5. Please report problems in the comments; attach [i]BepInEx\LogOutput.log[/i] if you can.

[h2]Changelog[/h2]
[b]v1.1.0[/b]: no hitches right after loading (the loading screen stays up until everything is loaded); buildings, trees and NPCs near the screen load a little at a time and NPCs load before they walk into view; no freeze the first time a worker starts a craft; garbage collection during door fades; no knock-on hitch after a slow frame; inventory window and chest item cells prepared in advance; a game update only turns off the affected fix
[b]v1.0.3[/b]: with No More Running Back, no ~0.25 s freeze when opening a chest in a big storage area like the yard
[b]v1.0.2[/b]: with No More Running Back, no second hitch right after a chest opens
[b]v1.0.1[/b]: removed the chest-window speed-ups (they could leave No More Running Back's queue next to chests empty); the pause menu's Report a bug button is hidden; no camera jump when opening a chest while walking
[b]v1.0.0[/b]: first release"
}
